2026-11-16 13:33:18 | RESPONSE | sactor.llm:160 | **Analysis of the unsafe parts**

1. **Null checks on `header` and `img_file`.** Crown reports both as single (`Ptr`), transient pointers. They are borrowed, not owned, and not arrays. In safe Rust they become `&_bmp_header` and `&mut W`, where `W: Write`. A reference can't be null, so the `HeaderNotInitialized` and `FileNotOpened` branches go away. The type system rules those cases out.
2. **`libc::fwrite` of the `u16` magic.** This becomes `magic.to_le_bytes()`, written through `std::io::Write`.
3. **`libc::fwrite` of the whole struct via a raw cast.** The fields total 52 bytes with no padding, so the C layout equals the fields written in order. I serialize each field explicitly with `to_le_bytes()`. This is safe, and it doesn't depend on the in-memory layout of the Rust struct.
4. **Return value.** `bmp_error::BMP_OK` becomes `Ok(())`. The original ignored `fwrite` failures. Here an I/O error is reported as `BmpError::Error`.

No `unsafe` remains.

----FUNCTION----
```rust
pub fn bmp_header_write<W: std::io::Write>(header: &_bmp_header, img_file: &mut W) -> BmpResult<()> {
    let magic: u16 = 19778;

    let mut buf: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(54);
    buf.extend_from_slice(&magic.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.bfSize.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.bfReserved.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.bfOffBits.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biSize.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biWidth.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biHeight.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biPlanes.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biBitCount.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biCompression.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biSizeImage.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biXPelsPerMeter.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biYPelsPerMeter.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biClrUsed.to_le_bytes());
    buf.extend_from_slice(&header.biClrImportant.to_le_bytes());

    img_file.write_all(&buf).map_err(|_| BmpError::Error)?;
    Ok(())
}
```
