2026-11-16 13:33:35 | RESPONSE | sactor.llm:160 | **Analysis of the unsafe parts**

1. `img_file.is_null()`: Crown marks `img_file` as a transient, mutable single pointer. It becomes `Option<&mut R>` where `R: Read`. `None` returns `BmpError::FileNotOpened`.
2. `libc::fread` of the 2-byte magic into a `c_ushort`: this becomes `read_exact` into a `[u8; 2]`, then `u16::from_le_bytes`. A short read or a magic other than `0x4D42` (19778) returns `InvalidFile`.
3. `libc::fread` of the whole struct through the raw `header` pointer: Crown marks `header` as a transient, mutable single pointer, and it is an out-parameter. It becomes the return value. I read 52 bytes with `read_exact` and decode each field with `from_le_bytes`, so no unsafe is needed. A failed read returns `Error`.
4. `bmp_error::BMP_OK` becomes `Ok(header)`, using `BmpResult`.

The decoding assumes little-endian, which is what BMP files use and what the original `fread` produced on common platforms.

----FUNCTION----
```rust
pub fn bmp_header_read<R: std::io::Read>(img_file: Option<&mut R>) -> BmpResult<_bmp_header> {
    let file = match img_file {
        Some(f) => f,
        None => return Err(BmpError::FileNotOpened),
    };

    let mut magic = [0u8; 2];
    if file.read_exact(&mut magic).is_err() || u16::from_le_bytes(magic) != 19778 {
        return Err(BmpError::InvalidFile);
    }

    let mut buf = [0u8; 52];
    if file.read_exact(&mut buf).is_err() {
        return Err(BmpError::Error);
    }

    fn u32_at(b: &[u8], off: usize) -> u32 {
        u32::from_le_bytes([b[off], b[off + 1], b[off + 2], b[off + 3]])
    }
    fn i32_at(b: &[u8], off: usize) -> i32 {
        i32::from_le_bytes([b[off], b[off + 1], b[off + 2], b[off + 3]])
    }
    fn u16_at(b: &[u8], off: usize) -> u16 {
        u16::from_le_bytes([b[off], b[off + 1]])
    }

    Ok(_bmp_header {
        bfSize: u32_at(&buf, 0),
        bfReserved: u32_at(&buf, 4),
        bfOffBits: u32_at(&buf, 8),
        biSize: u32_at(&buf, 12),
        biWidth: i32_at(&buf, 16),
        biHeight: i32_at(&buf, 20),
        biPlanes: u16_at(&buf, 24),
        biBitCount: u16_at(&buf, 26),
        biCompression: u32_at(&buf, 28),
        biSizeImage: u32_at(&buf, 32),
        biXPelsPerMeter: i32_at(&buf, 36),
        biYPelsPerMeter: i32_at(&buf, 40),
        biClrUsed: u32_at(&buf, 44),
        biClrImportant: u32_at(&buf, 48),
    })
}
```
